From: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 04:42:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: hotdog: derive image window from linked kernel

The fixed 0x01ad0000 image-size field matched the previously validated
kernel, but became stale as soon as built-in charger code changed the linked
image by 64 KiB. The bootloader places later payloads according to the actual
kernel length, while Linux requires the full advertised image window to remain
free. Keeping the old value can therefore overlap those payloads during early
boot.

Restore the standard linked size symbol so the header always follows
_end - _text as the kernel evolves.
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/head.S | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/head.S b/arch/arm64/kernel/head.S
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/head.S
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/head.S
@@ -147,7 +147,7 @@
 #endif
 	.quad	0x00080000			// Image load offset from start of RAM, little-endian
-	.quad	0x01ad0000			// Exact linked image window used by the proven V13 entry
+	le64sym	_kernel_size_le			// Effective linked image size, little-endian
 	le64sym	_kernel_flags_le		// Informative flags, little-endian
 	.quad	0				// reserved
 	.quad	0				// reserved
 	.quad	0				// reserved
-- 
2.50.1
